# fl-rifts lifecycle on a FIXED build (mod-fl-testbots; this folder must be listed in
# TestBots.ScenarioDirs). Start it right after a worldserver restart: the first player near the
# spawner 90018 (guid 5300694, map 727) opens a Rift of a random element at once.
# The director kills each wave with Xi'ri's Wrath (36944: instakill, every attackable enemy within
# 50 yd; the Rift itself is not selectable and survives), checks that the Rift closes as the boss
# dies, then waits 31 minutes at the hub (~600 yd away, out of the spawner's update range) and
# comes back. The next Rift must have opened meanwhile: Server.log shows "Closing completed Rift."
# before the stage 5 line and a new "Spawned rift" line between the stage 6 and stage 7 lines.
# On the unfixed build (07c7afa) the stage 5 checks fail (the Rift waits for the boss corpse) and
# no Rift opens before the director is back.
name    fl-rifts lifecycle - close on the boss kill, next Rift with nobody near
timeout 2400s
group none

place 727 12817.3 11967.0 -34.0
require gm alive
as gm .cheat god on
expect output has "Godmode is ON"
log stage 1 - at the spawner; the countdown of the new Rift runs
wait 125s
log stage 2 - wave 1
do gm cast 36944 triggered
wait 15s
log stage 3 - wave 2
do gm cast 36944 triggered
wait 15s
log stage 4 - boss
do gm cast 36944 triggered
wait 3s
log stage 5 - the boss died 3 s ago, the Rift must be closed
expect creature:90014 missing
expect creature:90015 missing
expect creature:90016 missing
expect creature:90017 missing
place 727 13421.8 11926.1 -32.9
log stage 6 - at the hub for 31 minutes, the next Rift opens meanwhile
wait 1860s
place 727 12817.3 11967.0 -34.0
wait 5s
log stage 7 - back at the spawner, a new Rift stands (see the Spawned rift line above)

cleanup
as gm .cheat god off
